<!-- yambox dual-arm cell: two YAM v1 arms with linear_4310 grippers and wrist-mounted Intel
     RealSense D405 cameras, plus a DECXIN camera looking down over the workspace, generated from
     yambox_linear_4310_d405_decxin.urdf (the source of truth) with the repo's standard URDF -> MJCF
     conversion. Kinematics only: no defaults, actuators, cameras or keyframe.

     The arms and their wrist cameras are byte-identical to
     ../yam_station_linear_4310_d405/yam_station_linear_4310_d405.xml, `right_base`'s 0.61 m offset
     included. Only the DECXIN, its cover and its bracket are modelled from the box CAD; the mast
     (`YB01_A01_010_cameraShaft`) the bracket clamps to is absent, and so is the bracket's own arm
     down to it, cut flush under the bracket's head plate. See README.md.

     `left_base` is the model root; `right_base` and `top_camera` hang off it as static bodies.
     Every arm mesh is referenced from arm/yam/v1/assets/ rather than duplicated here, and the two
     merged camera meshes live in ../assets/, with d405_wrist_linear_4310.stl shared with the YAM
     station.

     The `*_camera` and `top_camera` bodies are the optical frames (+Z along the optical axis,
     ROS/OpenCV convention) and each carries its camera assembly's merged mesh, so its <geom> needs
     no pos/quat: body frame, mesh frame and optical frame are one. `top_camera`'s quat includes the
     180 deg roll that takes the export's camera frame (+Y up) to that convention. See README.md for
     the extrinsics.

     `tcp_left` / `tcp_right` are the tool-centre frames, taken from
     gripper/linear_4310/linear_4310.xml's `grasp_site`: the flange turned 90 deg about Z and
     carried out to the centre of the two fingertip facets, 144.650 mm along the flange's +Z and
     0.104 mm off its axis. Measured from the tip meshes, and the same point at every finger
     opening because the fingers slide transversely. Sites are a MuJoCo concept, so the URDF has no
     counterpart. -->
